<title>SPAIN: Spain's bank Zaragozano H1 profit rises 21.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain's bank Zaragozano H1 profit rises 21.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Group results to end June 1997</p>
<p>				    (billion pesetas, unless stated)</p>
<p> Net attributable profit		 2.30   vs   1.89</p>
<p> Net interest income		    11.41   vs  11.13</p>
<p> Ordinary income			  17.13   vs  15.58</p>
<p> Net profit				  2.54   vs    1.98</p>
<p> Pretax profit			     3.42   vs    2.71</p>
<p> Operating income			  4.83   vs    3.86</p>
<p> Interest income			  26.23   vs   33.33</p>
<p> Interest expenses			15.11   vs   22.48</p>
<p> Net commissions			   3.83   vs    3.04</p>
<p> Financial/trading income		1.89   vs    1.42</p>
<p> Operating costs			  10.82   vs   10.42</p>
<p>    -personnel costs		     7.55   vs    7.30</p>
<p>    -other administrative costs	3.27   vs    3.12</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name Grupo Banco Zaragozano SA. The bank said it was calling an extraordinary shareholders meeting in October to propose an approximately three percent capital reduction.</p>
<p>It said it would pay a gross interim dividend of 48 pesetas, up 20 percent.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2151</p>
</text>
